01_whisperign_wall:
  No canary, no PIE, NX enabled.
  Program reads unlinited input into 16B buffer.
  We can find RIP offset and overwrite it with win address.

02_canary_callback:
  Canary enabled, no PIE, NX enabled.
  Program reads 128B into 64B buffer, overflowing into cast pointer.
  Then calls spell.cast, we don't need to touch the canary, we just need to overwrite cast pointer with win address.
